WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.981
If you placed Mount Everest at the

00:00:03.031 --> 00:00:05.287
bottom of the Mariana Trench,

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.318
its highest peak would still be submerged

00:00:08.368 --> 00:00:11.604
under more than two kilometers of water.

00:00:11.654 --> 00:00:13.187
Welcome to CurioSphere.

00:00:13.237 --> 00:00:16.346
Today, we descend into the deepest geological

00:00:16.396 --> 00:00:17.929
fracture on Earth.

00:00:17.979 --> 00:00:20.661
As you leave the sunlit surface,

00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:23.947
light disappears entirely within two hundred meters.

00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:26.254
At eleven thousand meters down,

00:00:26.304 --> 00:00:29.540
the water pressure exceeds one thousand atmospheres.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.571
That is equivalent to having the weight

00:00:32.621 --> 00:00:35.602
of fifty jumbo jets pressing against your

00:00:35.652 --> 00:00:36.652
chest.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.640
Yet, life thrives in the abyss.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.671
Specialized organisms produce piezolytes to prevent their

00:00:42.721 --> 00:00:44.679
cellular membranes from solidifying.

00:00:44.729 --> 00:00:47.710
We have mapped more of Mars than

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.500
our own ocean trenches.
